### Lab 5 - IntelliJ HTTP Client
### Configure JWT_SECRET and AUCTION_ADMIN_PASSWORD before starting.
### Username/password must satisfy lab4 registration rules.

### 1. Register - 201, accessToken and refreshToken
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"student18","name":"Student","email":"student18@example.com","password":"StrongPassword18!"}

### 2. Login - 200, accessToken and refreshToken
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"student18","password":"StrongPassword18!","deviceId":"intellij"}

### 3. Protected endpoint: replace ACCESS_TOKEN with accessToken from login
GET http://localhost:8080/api/security/me
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN

### 4. Refresh - 200, new pair. Replace REFRESH_TOKEN with refreshToken from login.
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken":"REFRESH_TOKEN","deviceId":"intellij"}

### 5. Replay: send same old REFRESH_TOKEN again -> 401; old session becomes REVOKED
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken":"REFRESH_TOKEN"}

### 6. Refresh used as access -> 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/security/me
Authorization: Bearer REFRESH_TOKEN

### 7. No credentials -> 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/security/me

### 8. Malformed token -> 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/security/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token

### 9. Ordinary USER cannot call admin API -> 403
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/admin/accounts/1/state
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"state":"LOCKED"}

### 10. Invalid login -> 401
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"student18","password":"wrong"}
